    "full_score_probability": 1,
    "hardest_part": "Surviving the early bootstrapping phase on a Death world marathon seed while every input costs a full real-time second: hand-mining enough iron/stone/coal, crafting a furnace and burner drill, and fueling/placing them before biters find the base. The UI-heavy parts (inventory crafting clicks, furnace fuel/ore slots, entity placement and rotation) are the most error-prone with one action per turn and no ability to pause while thinking.",
    "likely_failure": "Native character death to biters (or a biter chewing through the furnace/drill) during a stretch where I am stuck in menus or micromanaging mining, plus the 3-hour wall-clock budget expiring before automation is stable. A secondary failure mode is a soft-lock where I misplace or mis-fuel a furnace and stop converting ore to plates, capping the plate/gear milestones.",
    "helpful_mechanics": "Milestones are purely cumulative quantity thresholds, so slow but steady hand mining of iron ore banks many cheap points (1 through 100 ore); hand-crafting and smelting continue in the background while the character moves or mines; a single burner mining drill plus furnace converts free ore into iron-plate, gear and automated_iron milestones passively; the start area is usually biter-free for the first minutes and drills/furnaces are cheap.",
    "harmful_mechanics": "Death world biter aggression, fast evolution and expansion mean the base is under real-time attack while I am 'thinking'; marathon recipe and research costs slow every step; native death ends the only attempt; one input per second (and held keys being only 1s) makes mining and menu work extremely slow relative to the continuously running simulation; no pausing means any hesitation is punished."
